\f1\fs22 On the final chord, the performers advanced on the table and stripped it bare with all the greed befitting true rock-n-roll clergy. The guitarist flipped her instrument flat and loaded it with enough food to silence doubters. With arms and fretboards smeared in gravy, crumbs, and the inexplicable tang of bacon jam, the Elvi retreated, chewing the spoils.\
Sarah, not accustomed to threats wrapped as pop tunes, choked a little and levelled a killer stare at Chanta.\
\'93Don\'92t look at me, I didn\'92t write that!\'94 Chanta blurted. (In truth, he\'92d been workshopping nearly the same number with the musos all afternoon.)\
Captain Denver wrote in his notebook, with the gravitas of a bureaucrat signing away mines. He tore the page out neatly and placed it before Sarah, who half-expected an invoice.\
What chilled her stomach more than any Cloudborne debt collector\'97let alone an Elvi with expectations\'97was the actual message:\

\f3\fs18 By the authority of the Supreme Kingness, the High Elvis of the first Elvi Parliament of the Ghetto:\
You are confined to a term of convalescence until the birth of the esteemed Clinton.\
Thank you very much.
\f1\fs22 \
\
Sarah read it three times, jaw tight, brain gears grinding in neutral.\
Captain Denver suddenly perked up, raised a finger skywards as if recalling something, snatched back the note and scribbled with renewed passion on the flip-side. He handed it to her again.\
That, at least, Sarah understood.\
He\'92d given her his autograph.
